From 71d5b7fbf8136e91a0f9a2674f3e2ef58a9db791 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Osiecki <jesse@jjo.ninja>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:59:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add a configurable HOG detection threshold

dlib's HOG detector only reports faces scoring above 0. A face that is
backlit, in shadow or seen from below (tablet on the lap, window behind
the user) scores between -1 and 0 and is never handed to the recognition
model, so compare, add and the nod stamp all report no face at all.

Add detector.py with a thin wrapper around detector.run() that takes the
cutoff from a new [video] detection_threshold option (default 0, dlib's
behaviour) and use it everywhere a detector is built. The CNN path is
unchanged; the recognition certainty still decides whether the face is
the user's.
